# Pi with a shell, POSIX tools and curl, and no compiler: the README's "Pi with npm",
# whose page installs four device host modules: display, input, download for
# the download tool of Pi's Dolly extension (Janis links its client), and html
# for its ask_user and show_html tools (the html command). The recipe engine
# lets an npm user build an image FROM it (dolly-build).
INSTALL /v0.1.4/Dollyfile-core e5b08f1ce491828c25a7e7770a7eb5341abd53ad55919f6ce847ee5b8435dd5b
INSTALL /v0.1.4/Dollyfile-dollyfile ed34d6850478bb30dce74568c3e812c91e75e259bb9d02fd6f06cf0d8421fdef
INSTALL /v0.1.4/Dollyfile-posix 9aac98498e175e637b2bdfbfea7f366093c473aed04490c43bc5aedb32b6483d
INSTALL /v0.1.4/Dollyfile-display a56a0ac5a77b8fd936fe90ef5715b939683578e2d419ca021362b1c7baafd2f7
INSTALL /v0.1.4/Dollyfile-curl cd39deaca986f6c1b806d187156af1566a98a936458b66e43328265a9a2decf9
